<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Johannes Kepler</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1571">1571</a>–1630</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Johannes Kepler was a German astronomer and mathematician, born in the imperial city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/weil-der-stadt">Weil der Stadt</a>, who discovered the three laws of planetary motion. He served as imperial mathematician in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prague">Prague</a> and published the Rudolphine Tables in 1627. In 1628 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/albrecht-von-wallenstein">Albrecht von Wallenstein</a> brought him to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zagan">Żagań</a> in Silesia, where he set up a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/printing-press">printing</a> press; he died in Regensburg two years later.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/johannes-kepler.jpg" alt="Johannes Kepler" width="320" height="460" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: August Köhler [1] · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:JKepler.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
